    "fed_into_assembly": {
      "H1": "the family whitelists become `semantics.FAMILY_STRATEGIES`, which is the faithful extractor's `contract`: an inadmissible (code, extractor) pair is refused as a *stated obligation* by `semantics.inadmissible_pairs()` instead of a runtime raise.  It is also the `quits_faithful` counterexample's mechanism.",
      "H2": "the absence of any abstract interface in decoder/ is why the semantic layer must *check* R(c) rather than infer it like an effect system (PIVOT_NOTE section 8.5).",
      "H3": "noise being baked into the circuit is the `noise` coordinate in R(extractor) of every faithful assembly; its coordinate impact is {noise, extractor, decoder, experiment}.",
      "published_baseline_assembly": "source_faithful",
      "baseline_read_sets_from": "auto-extracted from the pinned QUITS tree by experiments/extract_read_sets.py (READ_SETS_FROM_SOURCE)",
      "baseline_edges_from": "auto-derived: ARTIFACT_READS_FROM_SOURCE minus self-loops (ASSEMBLY_EDGES_FROM_SOURCE): extractor <- code, arch <- code, decoder <- (code, extractor)",
      "hand_modelled_counterpart": {
        "assembly": "quits_dataflow",
        "read_sets_from": "hand-declared conservative H3 model: R(extractor) contains `noise` (build_circuit bakes the error model into the circuit) and R(decoder) is everything embedded in the circuit plus its own coordinate",
        "edges_from": "hand-set, deliberately over-approximating: extractor <- (code, noise); decoder <- (code, extractor, arch, noise); arch <- code (added 2026-10-09 -- the dynamic measurement shows a code substitution changes `layout_positions`, so this edge is real)"
      },
      "dynamic_cross_check": "experiments/dynamic_impact.json measures H1 and H3 by executing QUITS; that measurement is the ground truth, this file and extract_read_sets.py are the static cross-validation of it."
    }
  },
